  "articleBody": "Custom molding upgrades your home, but small oversights during planning or installation can ruin the visual appeal. Here are key pitfalls to watch for before starting your carpentry project.\n\n1. Skipping the material acclimation period. Bringing wood molding directly from a cold vehicle into a conditioned home and nailing it up causes gaps later when it shrinks. Give trim boards time to adjust to your home's indoor humidity.\n\n2. Overlooking room conditions. Installing moisture-sensitive wood stock in damp bathrooms often leads to buckling or warped seams. Choose materials engineered for moisture in wet spaces.\n\n3. Fastening too close to profile edges. Nailing right at delicate profile tips splits the wood and weakens the hold. Fasten into solid framing backings instead.\n\n4. Leaving uneven miter corners unaddressed. Walls are rarely truly square. Relying on simple 45-degree cuts without dry-fitting or coping creates visible seams that caulking cannot permanently hide.\n\n5. Painting before joints and fastener holes are properly sealed. Skipping thorough prep work leaves dimples and uneven lines visible under your topcoat.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\nIf your project involves complicated room transitions, uneven drywall, or high ceilings, bringing in a finish carpenter saves time and costly lumber waste. HH Remodeling LLC provides dedicated carpentry and finish work across the Denver metro. Call 303-505-0866 to get started.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
